# Rendered by Ansible on the target, never committed.
**/.env

# Vault password and any decrypted copy. The encrypted vault itself IS committed.
.vault-password
vault-password*
# A PATTERN, not the literal inventory/group_vars/all/vault-plain.yml this line
# carried until #641. generate-secrets.yml names its plaintext output after the
# artifact it becomes, so any renaming of that output -- the per-service
# vault_<role>-plain.yml shape #641 weighed, one file per service -- would have
# left plaintext credentials committable while this line still read as covering
# the generator's output. Unanchored like *.decrypted.yml below, so a plaintext
# rendering anywhere in the tree is ignored rather than only the one path the
# generator writes today; tests/policy_vault_test.rb derives the generator's own
# output name from the play and requires this to ignore it and its per-service
# variant. templates/vault-plain.yml.j2 is tracked and does not match, because
# a name ending .j2 does not end -plain.yml.
*-plain.yml
*.decrypted.yml

# Credentials and keys. The certificate belongs here beside its key rather
# than only the key: `tailscale cert <host>` writes <host>.crt AND <host>.key
# into the working directory, so ignoring one half left the other making the
# controller checkout dirty -- and roles/deployment_bundle refuses to deploy
# from a dirty controller, which stopped every five-minute poller tick with
# `?? as6704t-4043.tail4e1ae8.ts.net.crt`. A certificate is public, but it is
# host state and no more belongs in this repository than its key does.
*.key
*.pem
*.crt
**/secrets/

# Runtime data never belongs here
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.dump

# Local tooling
.ansible/
.venv/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.worktrees/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# .claude/ now holds one tracked thing, skills/, alongside two untracked ones.
# `.worktrees/` above does not match `.claude/worktrees/`, and until skills/
# landed nothing under .claude/ was tracked at all, so the directory was a single
# untracked line in `git status` that was obviously wrong to stage. Now it is a
# mix, and `git add .claude` or `git add -A` from the repository root would
# commit whole agent worktrees, each a second full copy of the tree, plus a
# settings.local.json carrying one machine's permission grants.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Optional copies of sanitized Mac proof evidence.
/mac-proof-reports/

# Local knowledge-graph output, regenerated on demand.
/graphify-out/
